solidity/out/
solidity/cache/
solidity/broadcast/
ts/node_modules/
ts/packages/*/node_modules/
ts/packages/*/dist/

# Generated from `forge build`, never committed. They are packaged into their
# published artefact (the crate embeds artifacts/ via include_dir! and binds
# abi/ with sol!, the npm package ships src/abis), so CI regenerates them
# before every build, test, dry-run and publish. Locally:
#   scripts/vendor-artifacts.sh     # -> rust/contracts/artifacts, rust/contracts/abi
#   pnpm -C ts codegen              # -> ts/packages/contracts/src/abis
rust/contracts/artifacts/
rust/contracts/abi/
ts/packages/contracts/src/abis/
ts/packages/contracts/src/calls/

# Vendored from the pinned libid-circuits release, never committed: the Honk
# verifiers and the platform table the circuits were built from (platforms.json,
# handles.json) are that repository's release assets, and circuits.json beside
# them (the version and each tarball's sha256, which IS committed) is the pin
# every download is checked against. CI's forge-build action vendors them
# before every build, test, dry-run and publish; the generators read the
# table. Locally, before `forge build` or a regen script:
#   scripts/vendor-circuit-verifiers.sh  # -> solidity/contracts/circuits/*HonkVerifier.sol, platforms.json, handles.json
solidity/contracts/circuits/*HonkVerifier.sol
solidity/contracts/circuits/platforms.json
solidity/contracts/circuits/handles.json

# Python bytecode from the generator scripts.
__pycache__/
